WEBVTT

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.000
The communicator was
intentionally destroyed?!

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.700
One of the people on
this ship is behind this.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.830
Kanata?

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.540
Wow! Too close!

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:12.160
Are you okay?
Are you concerned about something?

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.160
If there's anything you want to discuss,
you can tell me, alone, if that helps.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.410
We're companions, after all.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:22.790
Yeah.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.250
Aries Spring...

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:30.830
I was near her the entire time
the communicator was being destroyed.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:34.540
Or... Actually, she left my sight
when she was getting changed.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.950
Hey there, you two. How about a tasting?

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:45.330
Herb-grilled Tur-Gon breast and
suspicious scones with dried eccentric fruits.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.830
It looks delicious but sounds super weird!

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:49.700
I would love to!

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.580
The color of your eyes...

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.830
Yes, I was born with different colored eyes.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.330
Strange, isn't it?

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:06.540
I'm sorry I stared.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.700
They remind me of someone I know.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:13.950
Charce Lacroix. Well-versed in
biology and extremely smart.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.910
Good-looking and a great cook.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:18.040
Kind of annoying, when I put it that way.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.700
Ship maintenance complete.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.660
Okay.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:26.160
Zack Walker. Brilliant scientist.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.750
Since he found the broken communicator,
I don't think he's a suspect, but...

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:37.200
I need more time.
Let's observe the others a bit more.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.250
Thanks, Luca!

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:43.080
What are you guys doing?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.660
Look, look!

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.160
Wow! He made a hair ornament
out of that star flower!

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.120
I found some resin, so I whipped it up.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.790
Funicia Rafaeli. Quitterie's sister.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.040
She's only ten, so she's out of the question.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:06.250
Luca Esposito. He definitely has
the dexterity to pull off the trick, but...

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.120
You don't have a fever.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:14.290
I tried to check for unknown pathogens,
but you're fine.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.040
Must be fatigue.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.950
I'm sorry...

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:22.620
Don't apologize every time.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.290
It's just a coincidence
that I know about medicine.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.870
Take care of yourself.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.120
She's so gloomy.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.870
Quitterie Rafaeli.
Daughter of a famous doctor.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:41.500
She's the one complaining the most.
It seems unlikely that she did it, but...

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.290
Yunhua Lu.
Shy and never expresses herself.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:53.120
Seems harmless, but also the person
I know the least about.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.580
Argh! It's like...
everyone seems suspicious!

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.540
But at the same time not suspicious!

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.450
Ulgar.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.450
This is... the storage area.

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.120
What were you doing in there?

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.830
Did you find anything?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:24.200
Even if I did, I'd use it
to keep myself alive.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.790
I don't report to you.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:30.910
Ulgar, I don't mind that you don't want
to open up to the others, personally.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:35.160
But if there's anything you want to say,
you can tell me, alone, if that helps.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.870
We're companions, right?

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:40.620
Too close.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:45.040
Companions?
I haven't had any for 17 years.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.660
Stay away from me.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:58.000
I don't know who did it.
I have no idea why anyone would.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.580
Did someone really tamper
with the communicator?

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.330
No...

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:06.790
I can't be dwelling on something
I have no way of figuring out.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.910
We just need to get home safely.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.200
Safely...

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:21.000
"Planet Shummoor
Day 24 of being lost in space"

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.910
I've switched to normal drive.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:28.540
We'll be landing on
Planet Shummoor shortly.

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:29.660
"Hahaha"

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.290
"Hahaha"
What?! Nobody's listening!

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.500
--How long are you going to chit-chat?!
We're almost there!
--I lived in the countryside like you, Funi.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.410
--Come sit down, Mom.
--Oh, really?

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:38.450
I'm not your mom!

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:41.830
Aries, did you say you
transferred in June?

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.160
Yes.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:46.080
I was chosen as honor student
my second year,

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.700
and was allowed to transfer to Caird High.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.950
Funi, you came to my family
in June too, right?

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.160
Yeah.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.580
After my mother passed away in an accident,

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.870
I spent some time at an Organage.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.950
You mean "orphanage."

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:07.410
After a couple of days, some folks came
and said they found a family for us.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:10.450
Wasn't it surprising,
to be told that all of a sudden?

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:13.370
Not really, to be honest.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.250
The night I arrived at the place,

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:21.000
I got up at night to use the restroom
and heard some people talking.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.500
The headmaster was talking
to a man with sunglasses.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:31.500
They mentioned something
about me getting adopted.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:34.830
Really? On the same night
that you arrived? That's fast.

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:37.120
Maybe they knew beforehand?

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:41.700
Sunglasses-dude mentioned me, too.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:45.330
The dude in sunglasses
talked about the puppet?

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:49.000
Yeah, I didn't really understand what he said,

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:55.660
but it stuck in my head because he mentioned
"Animaroid B-5," Beego's show.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:58.040
I think he said...

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.790
"Put her on B-5 and we'll illuminate them all."

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.250
Huh? What does that even mean?

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.290
Get seated, everyone.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.330
It makes no sense.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:11.080
The guy in sunglasses said that?

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.120
Yeah.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.620
Put her on B-5...

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.040
Team B-5.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:24.080
Put her on B-5 and "eliminate" them all.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:32.910
Maybe they planned to put us on
the same team and kill us all in space?

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.950
Funi! Are you sure you remember
exactly what the man said?!

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.200
Yeah.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:45.450
If she's right, we weren't
selected randomly.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:50.080
We were chosen, deliberately,
to be killed all together.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:51.290
It can't be!

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:57.120
So, Funi getting adopted and Aries
transferring was all part of the plan.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:02.290
I wonder who this man
that Funi saw was.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.000
Maybe someone high up
in our school administration?

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.370
He has to be able to transfer students
and dictate who goes on what team.

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:11.290
Hey.

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:13.580
My father is vice-principal.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.910
Ulgar's father...?

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.790
Vice-principal?!

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.620
Hey! Is your dad a part of this?!

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.370
I don't know.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:28.830
But he's ashamed enough of his failure
of a son to hide our relationship.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:32.830
I wouldn't be surprised
if he wanted me gone.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.500
There's no point in rushing
to imagined conclusions.

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:39.120
We just don't have enough information.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:40.450
Kanata...

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:50.000
Guys, listen.
There's something you should know.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:55.870
One of us destroyed the communicator?!

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:58.500
How can that be?!

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:01.080
It's the logical conclusion,
based on observation.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.870
I don't want to believe it either...

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.910
Why would anyone do such a thing...?

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:08.950
If there really was a plan
to kill us all, it makes sense.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:14.160
One of us tries to kill everyone and
make it look like a camping accident.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.830
No!

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:20.120
Who?! Who is it?!
I can't sit around with a serial killer!

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:23.500
Why would anyone want to kill me?!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.450
No... No...

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.870
Quitterie, please calm down.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.290
Back off!

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.500
It could be you!

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.450
It's not me.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:41.120
Can you prove it?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.370
No.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.790
None of us can prove anything.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:53.410
Not under these circumstances...

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.160
That was me.

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:02.450
Under these circumstances?!

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:06.160
That was a stomach growl?!
Impressive, Aries!

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:09.120
I'm sorry. It's almost three pm.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.540
So it goes off at snack time?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:17.870
Kanata said, "hunger is the worst enemy."

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:24.250
Why don't we delay the landing a bit
and have a chat over some snacks?

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.290
Great!

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:28.000
Yes, let's do that.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.120
--I'll go get it.
--I actually have a new menu I'd like
you to try. I hope you like it...

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.200
--Snacks! Snacks!
--I actually have a new menu I'd like
you to try. I hope you like it...

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.580
--I'm hungry!
--Yes!

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.450
--Sounds good!
--Yeah!

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:39.160
I can't thank her enough, as always.

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:48.290
Charce, this is great!
Cereal bar with dried fruit.

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:52.620
I thought it would make
a good portable meal.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:55.620
Aries, back there, I...

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.700
Yes?

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.750
I'm sorry.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.700
No, it's natural to fall apart there.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.330
Chew or talk--pick one, not both!

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.660
Oh, which one should I pick?

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.870
Um, no...

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:11.950
Stay away from me.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:18.540
The accident that happened to this team
may have been part of a plan.

00:12:18.540 --> 00:12:22.950
Does anyone know why someone
would want us all dead?

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:29.120
Of course not. Maybe individually,
but not all of us at the same time...

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:33.290
Is there really a reason we'd
all have to be killed at once?

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:38.330
Was that sphere part of
the killer's plan, too?

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:47.250
The killer got sucked in, too. How did
the killer plan to survive in deep space?

00:12:47.250 --> 00:12:53.540
That's why they put the ship there!
It makes sense!

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:58.410
But the ship wasn't ready
for long-distance travel.

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:04.080
So then, how was the killer planning to
get home after successfully killing us?

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:09.250
Maybe the killer was on
the target list as well.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:12.290
You mean a suicide attack?!

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:17.290
I don't know why the killer did this,
or what they're living with,

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:20.330
but that's the only
explanation I can think of.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:26.080
If there really is a killer among us,
and they don't care about their own life...

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:30.160
They could try to continue
the elimination plan.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:35.160
If they don't care about their own life,
killing all of us would be easy.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:37.830
They would just need to disable this ship.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:53.830
What's going on?!

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.040
Not good!

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:57.660
There's a hole in the wall!
Air is leaking out!

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:59.910
The water server exploded!

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.660
The lights went out!

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:06.580
The lights are on!

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:10.200
We're floating!
Too much is happening at once!

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.200
What's going on?!

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:16.450
I don't know! The gravity generator
might have gone down!

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.950
Did someone use an explosive?!

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:24.660
This might be the cause.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:29.120
A meteoroid. We were hit
by flying space pebbles.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:33.250
The ship's deflectors are offline!

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:36.620
Good, so it's just an accident.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:39.080
My mistake. I'm sorry.

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:45.750
Survival tip number four! If we all work
together and help in different ways,

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.250
most things can be solved!

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.750
Vague!

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:51.120
Zack, go check out the gravity controller.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.040
Got it.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:55.700
Luca, you have a repair tool, right?
Can you plug that hole?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.250
On it.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:02.580
Yunhua, can you toss me my bag?

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.410
Oh, um...

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:12.290
Wow, you're really bad at attitude control!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:14.870
I'm sorry...

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.250
Whoa.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:21.910
It's like we're ballroom dancing, no?
Please rest, I can handle this.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:23.830
Enough with the charming prince routine!

00:15:23.830 --> 00:15:26.000
Here it comes, Luca.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.500
You're annoying!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.200
Behold, the glue gun,

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.370
and the instant hardening gel.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.950
It stopped.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:37.370
Smoothly done.

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.950
It's the only thing I'm good at.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:47.790
The bulkheads are fine...

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.660
Kanata, can you hear me?

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.870
Zack, how is it?

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:54.410
The walls were punctured here, too.

00:15:54.410 --> 00:16:00.620
The gravity controls are unharmed,
but the switchboard took a hit.

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:03.450
He said it'll take a while
to fix the switchboard.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:07.410
Hey, are you sure it's okay to land like this?

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:11.950
We should be fine to land, as long as
the gravity controls are fixed.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.250
The defunctors are back, too.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:15.450
You mean deflectors!

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:19.080
Hey, enough! Go and check
for other leaks or damage.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:20.870
I'm checking the air pressure in the cabin.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.750
Ugh, it's so hard to get around!

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.290
Stay cool, guys! Survival tip number nine:

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:31.080
Calmly solve each problem and all
problems will eventually get solved!

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.080
New problem!

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:33.790
What the heck is it, for crying out loud?!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.660
Kanata! Calm down!

00:16:35.660 --> 00:16:39.950
The <i>Astra </i>is getting pulled into
Planet Shummoor's gravity.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:45.080
We'll crash to the surface
if we don't do something!

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:48.160
How much time do we have?!

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:49.910
I'm calculating it now!

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:52.160
I can do it in my head!

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:57.750
Current altitude 1,550 km.
Planet radius, approximately 6,000.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:01.450
0.85G surface gravity...

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:04.910
About nine minutes, not including
time needed to decelerate!

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.750
Nine minutes...

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:10.120
Zack! Can you fix the power that fast?

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.200
No. Impossible...

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:18.250
We're done for. This is it.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.370
This is not it.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:27.540
I found a backup generator
near the food storage.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.040
Backup generator...!

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:34.500
Yes! We can connect a cable from
there to the gravity controller...

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:37.040
Then we can get it powered!

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:39.950
I found some cable rolls in storage.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:42.830
If we connect them,
we might be able to reach.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.910
Let's do it!

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:48.580
Yeah!

00:17:49.000 --> 00:17:53.620
Split up and connect the cables to
the backup generator and gravity controller!

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:55.410
Eight minutes.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:56.950
Assignments!

00:17:56.950 --> 00:18:00.080
Zack, take the helm and
control the ship's attitude.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:03.750
Luca, get to the gravity room
to plug the hole and boot the device.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:05.660
Funi, stay on the bridge.

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.450
Charce, go to the backup generator.

00:18:07.450 --> 00:18:10.750
The rest of you, pair up and
connect the cables to each other.

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:13.330
Okay. Move out!

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:15.700
I will...

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.040
Yunhua!

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.000
What's wrong?!

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:22.910
Yunhua is drowning!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.080
What?!

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.000
Hey! Are you okay?!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.750
I got this!

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:30.910
Everyone else, go ahead!

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:32.080
Understood.

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:34.870
We just need to suck
the water up with some cloth.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:37.080
Great work, young doctor.

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:40.750
If you can't do anything right,

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:44.500
the least you could do
is stay out of sight.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.950
The tears...

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:49.120
They won't flow...

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:53.750
You're an idiot.
Why don't you have your helmet on?

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:56.500
I'm sorry...

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:59.040
No, it's my fault for not instructing.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:01.160
Kanata, we have to hurry.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.200
Funi, pair up with Quitterie
and come with me.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.410
Okay.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:07.660
Yunhua, rest here.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.250
Hurry, hurry!

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:17.250
Hole plugged!

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:19.370
This way. Hurry up.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.370
Two minutes!

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:27.120
Cable A, connected to backup power!

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.750
Residential area, cables A and B connected!

00:19:30.750 --> 00:19:34.830
Engine area, cables B and C connected!

00:19:34.830 --> 00:19:36.620
Now it's just the gravity control room.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:37.790
Kanata!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:38.870
Luca!

00:19:38.870 --> 00:19:40.750
Here's the plug!

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:42.410
Connected!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.410
Send power now!

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:56.450
We made it! Gravity incoming!

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.750
What's wrong?!

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:01.250
We're getting an error!

00:20:02.580 --> 00:20:05.750
"Unidentified flying creature spotted"...?

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:13.080
What's that?!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:14.540
What's wrong?

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:17.410
There's a bird-like thing here!
It must have gotten in somehow!

00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:18.620
A bird?

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:23.000
It's a safety mechanism. If the system
detects something floating around,

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:27.040
it won't allow gravity generation.
Stop that thing or we won't make it!

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.870
No, we can't catch it with these thrusters!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.250
One minute!

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.450
We're so close...!

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.580
What are you doing?!

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:39.540
Ulgar!

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:42.410
Luca, hand over the glue gun!

00:20:43.790 --> 00:20:45.370
Brace and stabilize!

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:50.540
Can you shoot guns?

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:52.660
Shut up.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:53.950
We're counting on you!

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:55.870
I said shut up!

00:20:55.870 --> 00:20:59.910
I'm a self-taught shooter.
Don't expect too much.

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:05.160
Not a skill I planned to use on birds, but...

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.080
You did it!

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:16.580
Safety lock disabled!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:19.200
Gravity incoming!

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:22.870
<i>Astra</i>, full thrust!

00:21:26.830 --> 00:21:28.500
Hold on.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:32.040
Hold on!

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.660
We're safe now.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:49.910
Yes!

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:59.250
Yeah! We did it!

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:03.040
Great work, Ulgar.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:04.750
Shut up.

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:05.660
What?!

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:07.450
There, there.

00:22:07.450 --> 00:22:13.950
Ulgar's marksmanship was awesome!
If he had a real gun, he'd be invincible!

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:17.160
What are you talking about?
You read too many comic books.

00:22:17.160 --> 00:22:20.660
Guns were abolished, like,
a hundred years ago.
